---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Code.astro";
---
<Docs title="Using in plain HTML" lede="One stylesheet and one optional script. No build step, no framework.">
  <h2>A complete page</h2>
  <Code lang="html" title="index.html" code={`<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>My demo</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://dario-loi.github.io/polytope/kit/polytope.css">
  <script type="module" src="https://dario-loi.github.io/polytope/kit/js/all.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="ply-topbar">
    <div class="ply-container ply-topbar__inner">
      <a class="ply-wordmark" href="/">John Doe</a>
      <div class="ply-topbar__tools">
        <button class="ply-button ply-button--ghost ply-button--sm" data-ply-theme-toggle>Theme</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main class="ply-container ply-prose" style="padding-block: 3rem">
    <h1>My demo<span class="ply-stop">.</span></h1>
    <p>Body text sits in a column of about 68 characters.</p>
    <aside class="ply-note"><span class="ply-note__mark ply-note__mark--ball"></span>
      <div><span class="ply-note__title">Note.</span> Notes are mustard.</div></aside>
  </main>
</body>
</html>`} />

  <h2>Local copies</h2>
  <p>For offline work or a page that must never change, copy <code>dist/</code> from a release next to your page and point the links at it. The stylesheet finds its fonts in <code>./fonts/</code> next to it.</p>
  <Code lang="html" code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="./kit/polytope.css">
<script type="module" src="./kit/js/all.js"></script>`} />

  <h2>Only what you need</h2>
  <p>Each component also ships as its own file. Load the tokens first.</p>
  <Code lang="html" code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="./kit/fonts.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./kit/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./kit/css/base.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./kit/css/button.css">`} />

  <h2>Generated pages</h2>
  <p>Python scripts that write HTML (reports, experiment dashboards) can paste the same two lines into their template. The class names are stable within a major version.</p>
</Docs>
